sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task + full intent as inputs, single-swamp-node; DECISIONS 1 (token minted at admission, vault.get), 3 (automatic deploy = Gateway-published native schedule, no POST back), 4 / R1-R4 (process.stop shape); .env through the vault as in instance.create; rule 7 (reload over restart, restart_on_deploy only). docs/reference/deployments.md.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02, rules 21, 22 (automatic deploys only in instance.auto_deploy; cfgmgmt file/link/systemd, 0600 credential file for the fetch).
  %% status: draft
  %% command: instance:deploy
  %% kind: instance.deploy
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as app-prod Node<br/>Node 12 over ssh
  CLI->>GW: instance:deploy 42<br/>--commit=SHA
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit instance:deploy 42`
  %%> - syntax: `<instance> [--commit=SHA] [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the Instance; without `--commit`, the newest commit of its deployment branch
  %%> - `--commit`: a full commit SHA that must be on the branch's first-parent chain
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool send the same request
  %%> - automatic deploys start the same deploy steps from a native schedule; see the `instance.auto_deploy` chart
  Note over GW: Validate, freeze intent<br/>Instance 42 locked · task #5150
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to Node 12
  %%> - Instance 42 is an active production Instance of Project 7 on Node 12
  %%> - no other operation holds Instance 42; else `operation.target_busy`
  %%> Freezes:
  %%> - the branch and commit, the deploy steps, the shared paths and the release name
  %%> - the Project's Process and Schedule definitions and the PHP runtime
  %%> - the account `orbit-app-7` and its home `/home/orbit-app-7`
  %%> Renders .env:
  %%> - from the stored environment of Instance 42
  %%> Result:
  %%> - deployment 88 recorded as running; task #5150 recorded with the full intent
  %%> - a manual deploy pauses automatic deployment of Instance 42
  %%> - nothing has happened on the Node yet
  GW->>SW: Push token and .env<br/>vault: github-token, env-5150
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the repository is private, and only the Gateway holds the GitHub App key
  %%> - `.env` can hold secrets, which travel only through the vault
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - mints a read token for this one repository, valid 1 hour
  %%> - pushes the token and the rendered `.env` into Swamp's vault
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the run reads both with `vault.get`; no step calls the Gateway back
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-instance-deploy
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one run on Swamp serve (Node 209); every step runs there
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - Node 12's address and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
  %%> - the frozen intent; secrets only as vault key names
  %%> Budget:
  %%> - the sum of the deploy step timeouts plus 900 s
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5150
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task until it ends
  SW->>N: Prepare the release<br/>file 0600 cred · git fetch
  %%> How:
  %%> - Swamp reaches Node 12 over `@swamp/ssh` from 209; nothing is copied to the Node
  %%> - `@swamp/cfgmgmt/file` writes the vault token as a 0600 credential file; git reads it, so the token never enters argv
  %%> - shared paths and `.env` links with `@swamp/cfgmgmt/link`
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - fetches the branch into a new folder under `releases/` and checks out exactly the frozen commit
  %%> - refuses a commit that is not on the branch's first-parent chain (`deployment.commit_not_on_branch`)
  %%> - links the shared paths, the public storage link and each `.env` link
  %%> Runs as:
  %%> - `orbit-app-7`, through sudo
  SW->>N: Write .env<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/file · 0600
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - writes the rendered `.env` from the vault into `/home/orbit-app-7/.env`, atomically
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - restarts nothing; the running release keeps serving
  SW->>N: Run before steps<br/>@swamp/ssh exec · in order
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - runs each `before_activation` deploy step in order, from the new release, as `orbit-app-7`
  %%> - for example `composer install`, `php artisan migrate --force`
  %%> Limits:
  %%> - each step has its own timeout; a required step that fails stops the run
  SW->>N: Activate release<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/link · current
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - checks each served web root and its `.env` links in the new release
  %%> - replaces the `current` link with one atomic rename
  %%> Why:
  %%> - Caddy resolves `current` per request, so new requests use the new release at once
  opt Instance serves PHP
    SW->>N: Refresh PHP cache<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/systemd reload
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - converges the dedicated PHP-FPM pool of Instance 42 from the frozen PHP runtime
    %%> - reloads it gracefully, so running requests finish; then resets OPcache and waits for it
    %%> When a restart is needed:
    %%> - only when the pool's runtime itself changed, such as the PHP version
  end
  SW->>N: Restart Processes<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/systemd · forEach
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - installs the frozen Process definitions and the `laravel-scheduler` timer, in the `process.create` shape; other Schedules are native Swamp schedules and install nothing here
  %%> - for each running Process with `restart_on_deploy`: reload when the Process allows it, else restart
  %%> - for example Horizon: `php artisan horizon:terminate`, so jobs finish first
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - Processes without `restart_on_deploy`, and stopped Processes, stay as they are
  SW->>N: After steps, cleanup<br/>@swamp/ssh exec · keep 3
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - runs each `after_activation` deploy step in order, as `orbit-app-7`
  %%> - then removes old releases; the home keeps at most 3
  %%> Cleanup:
  %%> - best effort; a failed cleanup is a warning, not a failed deploy
  %%> - a release that a running process still uses stays
  SW->>N: Check the deployment<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt check
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - reads `current` back and checks it selects the new release and commit
  %%> - checks that each restarted Process is active
  alt all required steps pass
    N-->>SW: release, commit
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the selected release and its commit, and the restarted Processes
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event and reads the outputs; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record the deployment<br/>release, commit · task succeeded
    %%> Result:
    %%> - deployment 88 succeeds with its release and commit
    %%> - task #5150 succeeds
  else a required step fails
    N--xSW: exit ≠ 0 or timeout
    %%> When:
    %%> - a required step exits with an error, SSH fails, or the budget runs out
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed_step, selected release
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed, its error code and output tail
    %%> - which release `current` selects now
    Note over GW: Record failed deployment<br/>selection kept · task failed
    %%> Result:
    %%> - deployment 88 is marked failed; task #5150 fails
    %%> On the Node:
    %%> - a failure before activation keeps the old release selected
    %%> - a failure after activation keeps the new release selected
    %%> - Orbit undoes no step and no data change; the new release folder stays until a cleanup
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - deploy again after a fix; it is a new task with a new release
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5150
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status until it has ended
    %%> - the CLI uses Reverb events when the `websocket` role is active
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
